  "query_preview": "/WEDNESDAY NIGHT THROUGH MONDAY/...\nIssued at 200 AM CDT Tue Oct 6 2026\n\nThe warm and generally dry weather is expected to continue for\nlate in the week. There is a low chance (<20%) for scattered\nshowers late Thursday night into Friday morning as a bout of\nelevated warm air advection traverses the area. This is in\nresponse to a big shift in the upper-level pattern across the\ncontiguous U.S., as a deep upper trough digs into the Pacific\nNorthwest and surface cyclogenesis ensues across the Northern \nPlains.\n\nBy the weekend, ridging aloft will amplify across the Midwest as\na longwave trough sets up over the Western U.S. Therefore, \nexpect warm, breezy, and dry conditions for eastern Iowa and \nnorthwest Illinois with highs in the upper 70s to lower 80s.",
